    "id": "kata-dakuten-yoon",
    "day": 13,
    "title": "Katakana: ゛ ゜, small ャ ュ ョ ッ and ー",
    "explanation": "Katakana uses the same ゛ and ゜ marks and the same small ャ, ュ, ョ and ッ as hiragana, so ガ is ga, パ is pa, キャ is kya, and ッ doubles the next consonant: バグ (a software bug) vs バッグ (bag). The big difference is long vowels: instead of adding a vowel, katakana stretches a sound with a dash, ー, so ビル (building) and ビール (beer) are different words. Loanwords use ー for almost every long vowel, including the long 'e' in ケーキ (cake).",
